  "prefLabel": "En 402.14 Payphone",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 402.14 “Payphone” means any telephone made available to the public on a fee-per-call basis, independent of any other commercial transaction, for the purpose of making telephone calls, whether the telephone is activated by depositing coins, by calling collect, or by using a credit card.\n\nSource. #14015, eff 7-1-24 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for En 400)",
